MODIFICATIONS
-------------

This copy is NOT stock Chemprop. Three files were modified to add the PIPK-Net
mass-balance constraint:

    chemprop/args.py                  +7  -1   two new TrainArgs fields
    chemprop/train/run_training.py   +25   0   scaler threading, startup guard
    chemprop/train/train.py          +47  -1   the constraint term itself

Totals: 3 of 51 Python files changed, 79 lines added, 2 lines removed. Every
other file in this copy is byte-identical to upstream 1.6.1.

PATCH.md in this directory documents each edit, why upstream offered no hook
that could carry the constraint, and how the fork is kept off the import path
so that `import chemprop` continues to resolve to the stock installed package.

The modifications are released under the same MIT License as the original.
They are the work of the PIPK-Net authors and are not endorsed by, nor
associated with, the Chemprop authors or their institutions.

WHY A FORK IS REDISTRIBUTED AT ALL
----------------------------------

The published Chemprop benchmark figures were produced by stock 1.6.1 from
environment.yml, never by this copy. This copy exists only for the constrained
Chemprop arm, and is reachable only through
`python vendor/chemprop_physio/run_train.py`, which prepends its own directory
to sys.path. See PATCH.md for the verification that the two copies cannot
shadow each other.

Reviewers who prefer to rebuild the fork rather than take this copy on trust
can do so from the instructions at the end of PATCH.md; the diff above is small
enough to read in full.
